course: dictionary
lesson: 5580
title: The lever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lever is a bar that turns around a fixed point called the pivot. It helps you lift or move something heavy with less effort. «A see-saw, scissors, a bottle opener and a wheelbarrow all use levers.» Each one has a bar and a pivot, even when you cannot see them at first.
explain: The farther your push is from the pivot, the less force you need. That is why a long bar makes a heavy load easier to lift. «A seesaw is a lever with the pivot in the middle, so a child sitting far out can lift a grown-up sitting close in.»
explain: Lever is also a verb. To lever something is to move or open it using a lever, such as when you lever off a lid. A lever can also be a handle you push or pull to work a machine, like a gear lever.
fact: A lever is one of the simple machines.
fact: The pivot, or fulcrum, is the fixed point that the lever turns around.
fact: The farther your push is from the pivot, the less force you need to lift the load.
fact: «Levers» are used in scissors, bottle openers and wheelbarrows.
fact: «Lever open» means to open something by using a lever.
exercise: In «A seesaw is a lever with the pivot in the middle», what is the pivot? | The grown-up sitting close in | The bar that moves up and down | The child sitting far out | *The fixed point the lever turns around
exercise: What does a lever help you do? | *Lift or move something heavy with less effort | Change the colour of a object | Stop a machine from working forever | Make a loud noise
exercise: Which of these uses a lever? | *A wheelbarrow | A glass of milk | A soft pillow | A bowl of water
test: To lever off a lid means to | Paint the lid | Tie the lid shut | Shake the lid | *Move or open it using a lever
test: If you push a lever farther from the pivot, what happens? | The lever breaks | *You need less force | Nothing changes at all | You need more force
exam: Which statement about levers is true? | *A lever turns around a fixed point and makes a heavy load easier to move | A lever has no fixed point | A lever only works with water | A lever always makes things heavier
